WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.469
-President Trump has been
freaking out about

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.104
the possibility of a recession.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.940
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.776
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.677
♪♪

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:13.445
If there's one thing Trump
loves to brag about,

00:00:13.445 --> 00:00:14.780
it's the stock market.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.983
He talks about it constantly,
and by talks about it,

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.584
I, of course,
mean he lies about it

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.486
because he lies
about everything.

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:24.123
I would say lying for him
is as natural as breathing,

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.593
but he's not great
at breathing either.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.695
-[ Panting ]

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.763
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.498
-In fact, this week
the "Washington Post" published

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.068
an exhaustive study that found
that as of August 5th,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:38.537
Trump made over 12,000 false or
misleading claims as president.

00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:40.873
Which means that Trump said
something false about

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.175
once every three hours
on average.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:45.478
Once every three hours,
that means he has to wake up

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.647
in the middle of the night
just so he can get his lies in.

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:50.116
-"Russia's a witch hunt."

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.553
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.789
[ Applause ]

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.357
How does he even keep track?

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.225
He must have like a Fitbit
for lies.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.362
Like a -- like a Fib-bit

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.464
"Oh, no. I need to get my 10,000
lies in.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.065
I better hold a rally."

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.733
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.935
Trump's apparently told so many
lies that if he never told a lie

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.405
ever again in his life
he would still have average

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:16.375
8.7 untrue claims per day over
the span of his first term,

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.978
even though, under this
imaginary scenario,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.080
he hasn't said anything untrue
in more than a year.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.817
First of all, let's just bask
in that imaginary scenario

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.086
where Trump hasn't said anything
untrue in more than a year.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.622
I mean, imagine what his rallies
would be like

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.657
"Folks, people are coming
to the border

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:35.694
and they're seeking asylum,
which is perfectly legal.

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:37.430
And we should welcome them
because diversity

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.798
is our strength.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.834
Also, I'm terrible --
I'm terrible at golf.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.168
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:48.207
In fact, Trump gave --
Trump gave a speech on energy

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.076
to workers in Pennsylvania
on Tuesday,

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.245
and it was one reporters job

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.913
to basically sum
the whole thing up.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.715
It's what's known in politics
as the pool report.

00:01:56.715 --> 00:01:58.818
And here is the actual
White House pool report

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.286
summing up Trump's speech.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.822
"In a 60 minute speech,
that at times resembled

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.690
a campaign rally,
the President meandered

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.660
through several topics, meaning
have little to do with energy.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.863
He talked about trade,
immigration, trucks,

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:13.299
emoluments, his 2016 victory,
union leaders, his poll numbers,

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.935
the media, steel, China, the
amount of money he believes

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.137
he's losing as president,
the Green New Deal,

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:21.340
windmills, the WTO screwing us,
President Obama's book deal,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.108
Hillary Clinton's comments
on coal workers,

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:26.579
pipelines and New York, Iran,
veterans choice and more.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.880
Oh, my God.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.450
That sounded like a months worth
of "Jeopardy" categories.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.053
I'll take windmills for $400.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:37.223
The answer, this famous idiot
believe they cause cancer.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.225
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.862
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.397
Oof.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.899
They cause cancer.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:50.269
In fact, one of the lies Trump
told at that speech was about

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.204
the various lawsuits against
him, including a lawsuit

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.040
alleging that he is
violating a section

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.476
of the constitution that
specifically prohibits

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:59.111
what are known as emoluments
or gifts

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:00.280
from foreign governments.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.281
For example, a Saudi-funded
lobbyist paid

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:06.752
for 500 rooms at Trump's hotel
after the 2016 election.

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.854
Does Trump's hotel
even have 500 rooms?

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:11.290
I just assume there was a lobby,
and if you went upstairs,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.360
it was just fake doors painted
on the walls.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.895
Now, that seems like a pretty
clear violation

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.230
of the constitution,
and yet Trump

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.331
wasn't concerned about that.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.366
He complained instead
about how much

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.869
the lawsuits were supposedly
costing him.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.805
-This thing is costing me a
fortune being president.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.040
Somebody said, oh, he might have
rented a room

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.678
to a man from Saudi Arabia
for $500.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.980
What about the $5 billion
that I'll lose.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.151
It will probably cost me,
including upside, downside,

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:43.122
lawyers 'cause everyday
they sue me for something.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.892
These are the
most litigious people.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.827
It's probably costing me
from 3 to $5 billion.

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.931
-I don't believe you're losing
$3 to $5 billion from lawsuits.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.266
I would believe you're losing
$3 to $5 billion

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.235
just from, you now,
like being Donald Trump.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.305
I mean, you lost $1 billion
in ten years,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.806
and that was in
the '80s and '90s,

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.076
when everyone was making money.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:06.312
I mean, back then a little kid
could open a lemonade stand

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.014
and make enough money
to buy a Bugati.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:10.283
So Trump lies about everything,

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.551
and the stock market
is no exception.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.719
But if you compare his record to
the previous Presidents,

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.321
it's not as impressive.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.290
In fact, if you look at
the change in

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.959
the Dow Jones industrial average
over the same period of time,

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.161
Clinton saw 41.4 percent
increase,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.563
Obama saw a 41.7 percent
increase,

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.332
and Trump has seen
a 30.1 percent increase.

00:04:27.332 --> 00:04:29.535
So, Trump's been outdone by
Clinton and Obama,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.903
the two presidents
he hates the most.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.338
The only way that could be more
embarrassing for Trump

00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:35.608
is if he did loose
$3 to $5 billion

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.143
and they had to repossess
his penthouse

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.245
and rename it Hillary Tower.

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.846
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:43.282
More importantly --

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.719
more importantly, the stock
market is not the whole economy.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.287
In fact, most working people

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.223
aren't really invested
in the stock market.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:53.492
It's mostly just a sign at how
the wealthy few are fairing.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.729
In fact, one study found nearly
40 percent of the market

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.764
is owned by the richest
one percent of the population

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:01.133
while bottom 90 percent
of the population

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.469
owns just 19%
of stock market wealth.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.571
Basically, for a lot of people
the stock market numbers

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.506
in the bottom of the CNN corner
are just something

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:08.874
you staring at while
waiting for your flight.

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:09.975
It's like, "I don't know.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:12.711
I guess green is good
and red is bad.

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:14.213
I'm gonna go to the Cinnabon."

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.782
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.550
Trump's economic policy
has only benefited

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.985
the elite few to begin with,
and that a recession

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.954
seems like it might
be on the horizon,

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.290
he's freaking out because for
two years he's been able

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.827
to coast on the economic tide
left by Obama while ignoring

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.895
the growing wealth gap,
massive inequality

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:32.732
or the shuttering factories in
states he promised to rescue.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.468
In fact, Trump is so desperate
for something to brag about

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.336
that during that rambling speech
in Pennsylvania

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:40.540
he touted the Shell plant
that was about to open

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.575
and repeatedly claimed
credit for it.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:45.744
-This would have never happened
without me and us,

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.213
this would have never happened.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:50.216
It was the Trump administration
that made it possible.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.817
No one else.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:55.421
Without us, you would never have
been able to do this.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.822
-There you go.

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.090
The Shell plant would never
would have happened

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.691
without Trump.
Just one problem.

00:05:59.691 --> 00:06:01.627
Shell announced its plans
to build a complex

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.530
in 2012 when President
Barack Obama was in office.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.098
"Oh, it's been three hours.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.667
Better check my fib-bit."

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.769
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:11.703
I mean, he's taking credit
for a plant

00:06:11.703 --> 00:06:13.039
that was announced
when Obama was in office.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.073
What's next?

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.908
"Do you know I killed
Osama bin Laden?

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.576
I swear it's true.
I have --

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:20.213
I have a very real photo
to prove it."

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:23.048
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:25.985
Trump is freaking out
about the possibility

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:28.121
of a recession after spending
2 1/2 years

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.321
catering the wealthy elite.

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:30.956
He doesn't care about growing
inequality

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.291
or shuttering factories.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.527
We've got a lot of problems,
and in many cases...

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.361
-It was the Trump administration

00:06:36.361 --> 00:06:38.130
that made it possible.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.765
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:42.034
[ Cheers and applause ]

